    $n${"instruction": "Create a file called sample_transcript.txt and paste in the text below - a short, deliberately messy meeting transcript (someone joins late, and one task ends up with no owner) to test with. Swap in one of your own meetings once everything works.", "prompt": "Weekly Product Sync - Sept 1\n\nAttendees: Amaka, Tunde, Chidi, Priya (dialed in late)\n\nAmaka: ok let's get started, we're behind on the onboarding redesign.\nTunde: yeah the Figma files are done, dev just hasn't picked it up yet\nChidi: I can start on it Monday if nobody else is on it\nAmaka: sounds good, go ahead Chidi\n\nAmaka: also, we need to decide on the pricing page - do we keep the\nold three-tier layout or switch to the new single-price page marketing\nsent over?\nTunde: I vote we switch, the old one is confusing people, support tickets\nabout pricing are up like 30% this month\nChidi: agreed, let's switch\nAmaka: ok, decision made - we're moving to the single-price layout\n\nPriya joins late: sorry I'm late, what did I miss\n\nAmaka: quick recap - Chidi's starting the onboarding redesign Monday,\nand we're switching the pricing page to the single-price layout\n\nTunde: one more thing, someone needs to email the beta testers about\nthe pricing change before we ship it, don't want them blindsided\nAmaka: good call\nChidi: I don't think that's on me, I'm heads down on onboarding\nTunde: I can't this week either, I'm out Thursday and Friday\nAmaka: ...ok someone needs to own that, let's figure it out after the call\n\nAmaka: last thing - can we get the pricing switch live by end of month?\nTunde: should be doable, maybe the 28th\nAmaka: let's lock the 28th as the target then\n\nPriya: quick question, are we still doing the quarterly review next week?\nAmaka: yes, same time, I'll send the invite\n\nAmaka: ok that's everything, thanks all\n"}$n$, null),
  (4, 12, 'session', '{builds,0,steps,1,instruction}', '{builds,0,steps,1,instruction}', 'str', 'd7b9ad98fc6d20d9d6f9f49e5febd87c', null,
    $n$Create a file called make_samples.py, paste in the code below, and run `python make_samples.py`. It creates a sample_data/ folder with five short test documents - a business card blurb, an email signature, a job posting, a product review, and a real estate listing. Open them and skim them. Notice how differently each one is written; that's exactly the kind of messy, real-world text this project extracts from.$n$, null),
  (5, 12, 'session', '{builds,0,steps,1,prompt}', '{builds,0,steps,1,prompt}', 'add', null, null,
    $n$"\"\"\"\nCreates the sample_data/ folder this project reads from: five short test\ndocuments, each written in a very different style. Run it once:\n\n    python make_samples.py\n\nLater, drop your own .txt files into sample_data/ - main.py processes\nevery .txt file it finds there.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport os\n\nSAMPLES = {\n    \"business_card.txt\": \"\"\"\\\nSarah Okafor\nSenior Product Manager, Fintech Solutions Ltd.\n\nPhone: +234 803 555 0192\nEmail: sarah.okafor@fintechsolutions.ng\nLagos, Nigeria\n\"\"\",\n    \"email_signature.txt\": \"\"\"\\\nBest regards,\n\nDavid Chen\nAccount Executive | BrightPath Consulting\n\nMobile: (415) 555-2077\nEmail: david.chen@brightpathconsulting.com\nBook a meeting: calendly.com/davidchen\n\nThis email and any attachments are confidential and intended solely for\nthe addressee.\n\"\"\",\n    \"job_posting.txt\": \"\"\"\\\nWe're Hiring: Backend Engineer (Remote)\n\nTechNova Inc. is looking for a Backend Engineer to join our growing\nplatform team. You'll work on our payments API and internal tooling.\n\nSalary: $75,000 - $95,000 per year, depending on experience.\nApplication deadline: October 31, 2026.\n\nTo apply, send your resume and a short cover note to careers@technova.io.\nNo phone calls, please - we review every application by email.\n\"\"\",\n    \"product_review.txt\": \"\"\"\\\nProduct Review: The EcoBrew Coffee Maker\n\nThis coffee maker is made mostly from recycled materials and cuts\nbrewing time by almost half compared to our old machine. It has three\nbrew-strength settings and an auto-shutoff feature that has already\nsaved us from a couple of forgetful mornings.\n\nThe water tank could be a little bigger, and the instructions that came\nin the box were confusing, but overall this is a solid choice for anyone\nlooking to reduce their environmental footprint without sacrificing\ntheir morning routine.\n\"\"\",\n    \"real_estate_listing.txt\": \"\"\"\\\nFOR SALE: 3-Bedroom Duplex, Lekki Phase 1, Lagos\n\nPrice: NGN 85,000,000 (negotiable)\n\nSpacious 3-bedroom duplex with a boys' quarters, fitted kitchen, and\n24-hour power backup. Gated estate with 24/7 security.\n\nListed on: 2026-08-15\n\nContact the agent, Chidinma Eze, on 0807 123 4567 for a viewing.\nSerious inquiries only, please.\n\"\"\",\n}\n\nos.makedirs(\"sample_data\", exist_ok=True)\nfor name, text in SAMPLES.items():\n    with open(os.path.join(\"sample_data\", name), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        f.write(text)\nprint(f\"Created sample_data/ with {len(SAMPLES)} files.\")\n"$n$, null),
